{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the ark rested in the seventh month, on the seventeenth day of the month, upon the mountains of Ararat.</b> The day of the ark's rest was on the seventeenth of Nisan. And as for what Scripture says, ״ויגברו המים על הארץ חמשים ומאת יום״ — 'and the waters prevailed upon the earth a hundred and fifty days' — this prevailing began on the seventeenth of Marcheshvan, as it is written, ״בשנת שש מאות שנה לחיי נח בחדש השני בשבעה עשר יום לחדש נבקעו כל מעינות תהום״ — 'In the six hundredth year of Noah's life, in the second month, on the seventeenth day of the month, were all the fountains of the great deep broken up' etc. From the seventeenth of Marcheshvan to the seventeenth of Nisan you will find ק״נ (150) days." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote:</b> The order in this matter was that on the day the rain descended, the fountains of the deep were broken up and the windows of heaven were opened, and the rain came down forty days; and during them the waters prevailed fifteen cubits above, and the rain ceased at the end of forty, but the fountains of the deep and the windows of heaven remained open, and the air was very damp and all the earth was filled with water and would never dry, and they stood thus in their might for 150 days from the descent of the rain. Then the Holy One, blessed be He, brought a very mighty wind through the heavens and the earth, and the fountains of the deep were stopped up, for the natural waters returned to their place until the deep was filled as it had been at first, and the openings of the fountains were closed, and the windows of heaven were closed, and the air dried greatly through the drying wind. And so the waters diminished a great deal, and the ark rested — it had been submerged in the water by two or three cubits. And after 73 days, on the first day of the tenth month, which is the month of Tammuz, the tops of the mountains were seen. And at the end of forty days that he waited after the tops of the mountains were seen to him — this falls on the tenth of Av — he opened the window of the ark. And after three weeks the dove went forth from him, and after thirty he removed the covering of the ark. End of quote."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:16.208615255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}